      "status": "supported",
      "text": "certiorari to the united states court of appeals for the third circuit No. 22\u2013174. Argued April 18, 2023\u2014Decided June 29, 2023"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner Gerald Groff",
      "case_id": "2022-22-174",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b17b9d84575b1bb6590eea103149bd43253bdf6004f2152b7193d2ff0b0930e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b17b9d84575-0000-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Groff sued under Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, asserting that USPS could have accommodated his Sunday Sabbath practice \u201cwithout undue hardship on the conduct of [USPS's] business.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-22-174",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b17b9d84575b1bb6590eea103149bd43253bdf6004f2152b7193d2ff0b0930e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b17b9d84575-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Solicitor General Prelogar argued the cause for respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-174",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b17b9d84575b1bb6590eea103149bd43253bdf6004f2152b7193d2ff0b0930e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b17b9d84575-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We granted Groff's ensuing petition for a writ of certiorari."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "TWA",
      "case_id": "2022-22-174",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b17b9d84575b1bb6590eea103149bd43253bdf6004f2152b7193d2ff0b0930e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b17b9d84575-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Summary of Argument in TWA's brief began with this categorical assertion: \u201cThe religious accommodation requirement of Title VII violates the Establishment Clause of the First Amendment.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-174",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b17b9d84575b1bb6590eea103149bd43253bdf6004f2152b7193d2ff0b0930e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b17b9d84575-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court held that Title VII imposed no such requirement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-174",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b17b9d84575b1bb6590eea103149bd43253bdf6004f2152b7193d2ff0b0930e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b17b9d84575-0001-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Marshall suggested one possible reason: that the collective bargaining agreement might have disallowed Hardison's working overtime for regular wages."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-174",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b17b9d84575b1bb6590eea103149bd43253bdf6004f2152b7193d2ff0b0930e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b17b9d84575-0001-0005",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "To require TWA to bear more than a de minimis cost in order to give Hardison Saturdays off is an undue hardship."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner Groff",
      "case_id": "2022-22-174",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b17b9d84575b1bb6590eea103149bd43253bdf6004f2152b7193d2ff0b0930e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b17b9d84575-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Both parties agree that the \u201cde minimis\u201d test is not right, but they differ slightly in the alternative language they prefer. Groff likes the phrase \u201csignifcant diffculty or expense.\u201d Brief for Petitioner 15; Reply Brief 2."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-174",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b17b9d84575b1bb6590eea103149bd43253bdf6004f2152b7193d2ff0b0930e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b17b9d84575-0002-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The erroneous de minimis interpretation of Hardison may have had the effect of leading courts to pay insuffcient atten- tion to what the actual text of Title VII means with regard"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-174",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b17b9d84575b1bb6590eea103149bd43253bdf6004f2152b7193d2ff0b0930e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b17b9d84575-0002-0005",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The judgment of the Court of Appeals is vacated, and the case is remanded for further proceedings consistent with this opinion. It is so ordered."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-174",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b17b9d84575b1bb6590eea103149bd43253bdf6004f2152b7193d2ff0b0930e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b17b9d84575-0002-0001",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As both parties here agree, the phrase \u201cmore than a de minimis cost\u201d from Trans World Airlines, Inc. v. Hardison, 432 U. S. 63, 84 (1977), was loose language. An employer violates Title VII if it fails \u201cto reasonably accommodate\u201d an employee's religious observance or practice, unless the employer demonstrates that accommodation would result in \u201cundue hardship on the conduct of the employer's business.\u201d 42 U. S. C. \u00a7 2000e(j). The statutory standard is \u201cundue hardship,\u201d not trivial cost."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-174",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b17b9d84575b1bb6590eea103149bd43253bdf6004f2152b7193d2ff0b0930e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b17b9d84575-0003-0000",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "To be sure, some effects on co-workers will not constitute \u201cundue hardship\u201d under Title VII. For example, animus to- ward a protected group is not a cognizable \u201chardship\u201d under any antidiscrimination statute."
    },
